Changes made by Renown relative to PecoFence:

  * The Direct2D/Composition renderer (`crates/render`) is not used. Fence
    windows are drawn by a React 19 frontend running inside Tauri/WebView2.
  * The `platform`, `app`, `cli`, `ipc` and `watchdog` crates were not copied
    wholesale; only the portable logic was re-implemented in
    `src-tauri/src/fence/`:
      - `model.rs`   — fence/item/layout data model
      - `rules.rs`   — rule engine (schemars and i18n removed)
      - `desktop.rs` — desktop folder enumeration and item merging
      - `icons.rs`   — IShellItemImageFactory icon extraction and disk cache
      - `monitor.rs` — monitor enumeration and layout fingerprint matching
      - `window.rs`  — Progman/WorkerW discovery, icon hiding, z-order
      - `shortcut.rs`— `.lnk`/`.url` target parsing (binary MS-SHLLINK parser
                       instead of the IShellLink COM interface)
  * The configuration format was changed (UUID-keyed maps, `AssignedBy::Default`
    added so the rule engine can take over default-routed items).
  * The CLI, AI-agent integration, portal fences and the watchdog process are
    not implemented.

